Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0;font-size:10px;max-width:260px;line-height:1.3">This is the phase diagram of water. The three red curves separate solid (s), liquid (l), and vapor (v) regions. Use the steps to explore how the state point's position determines the phase.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:4px;align-items:center;margin:2px 0">
<button onclick="prevStep()" style="padding:2px 8px">◀</button>
<span id="stepLabel" style="font-size:10px">1/5</span>
<button onclick="nextStep()" style="padding:2px 8px">▶</button>
</div>
<label>Temperature T (°C): <output id="temperatureVal">25</output>
<input id="temperatureInput" type="range" min="-10" max="400" step="1" value="25" oninput="document.getElementById('temperatureVal').value=this.value;update_temperature(+this.value)"></label>
<label>Pressure p (atm): <output id="pressureVal">1</output>
<input id="pressureInput" type="range" min="0" max="250" step="0.5" value="1" oninput="document.getElementById('pressureVal').value=this.value;update_pressure(+this.value)"></label>
